    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0666" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 814.51/210.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Guatemalan Government has been informed that the British Government refuses
                    to consider a just arrangement for converting the external debt of Guatemala and
                    thereby make it possible to reorganize the finances and currency of that
                    country, and is painfully surprised thereat. If the Department considers it
                    advisable the Guatemalan Government will send a special financial and diplomatic
                    agent to London. The Foreign Office desires to know whether you have any advices
                    since December 28, 1912.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hitt</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
